&lt;p&gt;MongoDB is seeking a Senior Workplace Coordinator to support the Austin office and help create a workplace experience that is welcoming, productive, and energizing for employees and visitors alike.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is ideal for someone who enjoys being the go-to person, thrives in a fast-moving environment, and takes pride in bringing people together. While this is a broad workplace coordination role, event planning and execution will be a major focus. You will help shape a vibrant office culture by leading workplace-supported events and experiences while also supporting the day-to-day operations that keep the office running smoothly.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;No two days are the same. One day, you may be planning an office-wide celebration, coordinating vendors, and managing event logistics. Next, you may be responding to employee requests, reviewing space setups, supporting visitors, or partnering with local teams to ensure the office is operating at a high standard. If you are organized, proactive, service-minded, and excited by both hospitality and operations, this could be a great fit.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the planning and execution of workplace-supported events, activations, and office experiences, bringing a Think Big, Go Far mindset to programming that strengthens culture and connection&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Employee Experience, Recruiting, Executive Assistants, ERGs, Site Leadership, and other cross-functional teams to Build Together and deliver thoughtful programming&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage event logistics from concept through execution, including vendor coordination, catering, timelines, communications, room setup, onsite support, and follow-up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make it Matter by delivering events that are elevated, organized, purposeful, and aligned with the employee experience goals, budgets and local flare of the Austin office&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own What You Do by helping ensure the office is operated and maintained in a safe, professional, organized, clean, and efficient manner&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the front-of-house experience by greeting employees, visitors, guests, and vendors with warmth and a hospitality-first mindset&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Respond to, track, and resolve employee requests through internal workplace support channels and systems with urgency, follow-through, and accountability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct regular walkthroughs of the office to identify operational, maintenance, hospitality, or presentation issues and follow through on needed actions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor office supplies and coordinate replenishment weekly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage vendor relationships for cleaning, lunch delivery, maintenance, compliance and office services&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate workplace updates, expectations, and event information clearly and consistently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a visible, approachable point of contact for workplace support in Austin&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be Intellectually Honest when assessing office needs, identifying patterns, escalating issues, and recommending practical improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support tracking of workplace spending related to events, supplies, and office operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Balance creativity with practical decision-making to deliver meaningful employee experiences within budget constraints&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Requirements&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in workplace, office coordination, hospitality, events, employee experience, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong event planning and execution experience, ideally in an office, hospitality, or employee-facing environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent organizational skills, follow-through, and attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proactive, hands-on approach and the ability to manage multiple priorities in a dynamic environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills and confidence working with a wide range of stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A warm, service-oriented mindset with strong emotional intelligence and sound judgment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with vendors, budgets, and administrative processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with workplace technology and productivity tools, including Google Workspace and Microsoft Office&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work onsite in the Austin office on a consistent basis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lift and move up to 30 lbs when needed for event setup or workplace support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;About MongoDB&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;MongoDB is built for change, empowering our customers and our people to innovate at the speed of the market. We have redefined the data platform for the AI era, enabling builders to create, transform, and disrupt industries with software. MongoDB’s unified data platform, the most widely available, globally distributed data platform on the market, helps organizations modernize legacy workloads, embrace innovation, and unleash AI. Our cloud-native platform, MongoDB Atlas, is the only globally distributed, multi-cloud data platform and is available across AWS, Google Cloud, and Microsoft Azure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;With offices worldwide and over 67,000 customers, including 75% of the Fortune 100 and AI-native startups, relying on MongoDB for their most important applications, we’re powering the next era of software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our compass at MongoDB is our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mongodb.com/company&quot;&gt;Leadership Commitment,&lt;/a&gt; guiding how and why we make decisions, show up for each other, and win. It’s what makes us MongoDB.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To drive the personal growth and business impact of our employees, we’re committed to developing a supportive and enriching culture for everyone. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mongodb.com/company/blog/culture/employee-benefits-that-make-a-difference-at-mongodb&quot;&gt;From employee affinity groups, to fertility assistance and a generous parental leave policy&lt;/a&gt;, we value our employees’ wellbeing and want to support them along every step of their professional and personal journeys.&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mongodb.com/blog/channel/culture&quot;&gt; Learn more about what it’s like to work at MongoDB&lt;/a&gt;, and help us make an impact on the world!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;MongoDB is committed to providing any necessary accommodations for individuals with disabilities within our application and interview process. To request an accommodation due to a disability, please inform your recruiter.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;MongoDB, Inc. provides equal employment opportunities to all employees and applicants for employment and prohibits discrimination and harassment of any type and makes all hiring decisions without regard to race, color, religion, age, sex, national origin, disability status, genetics, protected veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state or local laws.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Req ID: 2273498900&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;MongoDB’s base salary range for this role is posted below. Compensation at the time of offer is unique to each candidate and based on a variety of factors such as skill set, experience, qualifications, and work location. Salary is one part of MongoDB’s total compensation and benefits package. Other benefits for eligible employees may include: equity, participation in the employee stock purchase program, flexible paid time off, 20 weeks fully-paid gender-neutral parental leave, fertility and adoption assistance, 401(k) plan, mental health counseling, access to transgender-inclusive health insurance coverage, and health benefits offerings. Please note, the base salary range listed below and the benefits in this paragraph are only applicable to U.S.-based candidates.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;MongoDB’s base salary range for this role in the U.S. is:&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$45,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$88,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
